clean_summary:
A good time to reflect on how it took two more years for people to begin waking up.

@paulg: "Imagine what it will be like if five years from now models have improved on Fable as much as Fable has improved on GPT-3."

The linked article discusses the scaling hypothesis, which suggests that neural networks absorb data and compute, generalize, and become more Bayesian as problems get harder. This leads to new abilities emerging even at scales considered trivial by global standards, indicating that deep learning's revolution has begun as predicted.
